From 93cbfbda08f91693a7c9bbb1ef9eb8df14860333 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Diego Amicabile <diego.amicabile@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 07:35:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Borg: skip an unidentified item when counting things to sell

borg_count_sell() counts the pack items worth selling; the result decides
whether a low-level borg should stop diving and go to town to sell
(count of 13 or more).  On an unidentified item that is not part of a
stack it returned false -- a count of 0 -- instead of skipping that one
item, and it left the borg's traits as computed for its last trial
removal (the final borg_notice() was skipped).

So one unidentified item made a full pack look empty, and the borg kept
taking down staircases instead of going up to sell.

Skip the item with 'continue', as the surrounding filters do.

Tracked as diegoami/neo-angband-tracker#134.

(cherry picked from commit 026a42d3fcdfcbedaaef12c6f39200e38ecbd2ed)
---
 src/borg/borg-store-sell.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/borg/borg-store-sell.c b/src/borg/borg-store-sell.c
index 9fcfd53b3..906d5826a 100644
--- a/src/borg/borg-store-sell.c
+++ b/src/borg/borg-store-sell.c
@@ -1221,7 +1221,7 @@ int borg_count_sell(void)
         if (borg_item_note_needs_id(item)) {
             /* note if we have more than one */
             if (!borg_has_mutiple(item))
-                return false;
+                continue;
         }
 
         /* Don't sell my needed potion/wands/staff/scroll collection */
-- 
